{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"snug-undesired-oryx","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n`docs/ticket-model.md:288` and the comment `src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py:200-203` say `edit_ticket(tags=…)` is a deprecated alias; it was removed (`composer_edit.py:301-302`, CLI refusal `:422-426`; MCP `edit_ticket` has only `add_tags/remove_tags/set_tags`, `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:361-380`). `docs/plan-review-gate.md:113,122-123,1158,1183` teach `[operator-attested]`; ADR 0101 (`:33-49`) makes `[non-codebase]` canonical and keeps the old spelling as an accepted, UNDOCUMENTED alias (`tests/unit/test_guides.py:84-91` enforces this for the packaged guide). `docs/migrations.md:99` cites `init.py` for the ensure units, which live in `src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py` (reachable as `init._<name>`, pinned by `tests/unit/test_init_ensures_seam.py:10-14`); `:256,:264,:293` cite bare `compact.py`/`_processors.py` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact.py`, `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`).\n\n## Approach\n- `docs/ticket-model.md:288-289` → \"The library/MCP `edit_ticket(tags=…)` set-alias was removed pre-1.0; `tags` is rejected as an unknown edit field — use `add_tags` / `remove_tags` / `set_tags`.\"\n- `composer_edit.py:200-203` → `# Tags are NOT an EDIT field (P2.3): they mutate via TAG_DELTA deltas` / `# (--add-tag/--remove-tag/--set-tags), so a whole-field EDIT can never clobber a` / `# concurrent tag add. The library/MCP edit_ticket(tags=...) set-alias was removed` / `# pre-1.0 (DE7); \"tags\" is now an unknown field, refused below.`\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md`: `:113` \"NOT tagged `[operator-attested]`\" → \"NOT tagged `[non-codebase]` (ADR 0101)\"; `:122-123` \"The `[operator-attested]` tag matcher is single-sourced in `det_operator_attested` (`_OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE`…\" → \"The `[non-codebase]` tag matcher (which also accepts the legacy spelling) is single-sourced in `det_operator_attested` (`_OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE`…\" (symbol names are real, keep them); `:1158` \"Items whose text begins with the `[operator-attested]` tag (ADR-0043)\" → \"…the `[non-codebase]` tag (ADR-0043, renamed by ADR 0101)\"; `:1183` \"an `[operator-attested]` AC item\" → \"a `[non-codebase]` AC item\". Leave `:472` (a fixture name).\n- `docs/migrations.md:99` → \"(`_commands/init.py` is the entry point; the units themselves live in `_commands/_init_ensures.py` and stay reachable as `init._<name>`)\"; `:256,:264` `compact.py` → `_commands/compact.py`; `:260,:293` `_processors.py` → `reducer/_processors.py`.\n\n## Scope\n`docs/ticket-model.md`, `src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py` (comment only), `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/migrations.md`. Not: `docs/config.md` (config epic), `docs/adr/0086…:67` (overlap epic), `docs/adr/0059…:1009` (historical).\n\n## Testing\n`make lint` (ruff, comment hygiene, complexity ratchet — comment-only change scores nothing); `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check`; `pytest tests/unit/test_gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_unlink_documentation_contract_b6e1.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_docs.py tests/unit/test_plan_review.py tests/unit/test_s4_prompt_cutover_edge.py tests/unit/test_project_portability_docs.py tests/unit/test_det_floor_clarity.py tests/unit/test_llm_model_env_removal.py tests/unit/test_guides.py tests/unit/test_init_ensures_seam.py tests/unit/test_gen_ticket_model_taxonomy.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `grep -n 'deprecated alias' docs/ticket-model.md src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py` is empty.\n- [ ] `grep -c '\\[operator-attested\\]' docs/plan-review-gate.md` = 0 and `grep -c '\\[non-codebase\\]' docs/plan-review-gate.md` ≥ 5 (four rewrites + `:318`).\n- [ ] `grep -n '`init.py`\\|`compact.py`\\|`_processors.py`' docs/migrations.md` is empty; `git diff --stat -- src` shows only comment lines (`git diff -U0 -- src | grep '^[-+]' | grep -v '^[-+][-+]' | grep -v '^[-+]\\s*#'` empty).","id":"28d0-148d-43a6-4e5e","parent_id":"cdac-532f-0edb-422d","priority":3,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Fix the doc drift the census found: removed tags alias, [non-codebase] spelling, moved module paths"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788808186447398375,"uuid":"c106e14a-7d46-430c-b417-d4182e3d4020"}